@startuml
title Existing durable operation states / UI overlays — DRAFT
state "Starting / reconciling\n(local observation only)" as Starting
state "running\n(server persisted)" as Running
state "completed" as Completed
state "failed\nINTERRUPTED is a reason" as Failed
state "cancelled" as Cancelled
[*] --> Starting : explicit command / known key
Starting --> Running : server claim found
Starting --> Completed : completed record found
Starting --> Failed : failed record found
Starting --> Cancelled : cancelled record found
Running --> Completed : server success wins race
Running --> Failed : server failure / process interruption
Running --> Cancelled : server cancellation confirmed
Completed --> [*]
Failed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
note right of Running
Cancellation request keeps running state
until server confirms the actual result.
Read failure is a stale/unavailable overlay,
not an operation-state transition.
No queued, pause or generic resume state.
end note
note bottom of Failed
Retry, when permitted, creates a separate execution
with a new key after outcome reconciliation.
end note
@enduml
